# HTML markup — minimize nesting

All else being equal, prioritize fewer nested HTML elements.

If styling can be accomplished with one wrapper, prefer that over a wrapper plus an inner wrapper.

## This project

- **Layout column**: `.content` — max-width, centering, horizontal padding.
- **Full-bleed band**: combine on one element — `.content.band.band-steel` — not `.band > .content`.
- **Section grouping**: use semantic `<section>` directly; no redundant wrapper classes.
- **Exception**: keep an extra wrapper only when required (e.g. `.hero-slot` for quote overlay positioning, `.band__body` for two-column band layout).

## Examples

```html
<!-- Prefer -->
<div class="content band band-steel">
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>…</p>
</div>

<!-- Avoid when one element suffices -->
<div class="band band-steel">
  <div class="content">…</div>
</div>
```

When adding a new pattern, reach for combined classes or pseudo-elements (`::before` for full-bleed backgrounds) before introducing another DOM layer.
